Subject: an implied object schema must not override the caller's grammar

Upstream now turns the empty schema of a bare response_format json_object
into {"type": "object"} (acecd5603), which fixes what this stack's earlier
patch fixed. It does so unconditionally, though, and a schema beats a grammar
downstream (common/chat.cpp), so a request carrying its own `grammar` plus a
bare json_object loses the grammar. Leave the schema empty in that case, as
the stack's patch did since its first rebuild.

--- a/tools/server/server-common.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-common.cpp
@@ -1320,7 +1320,11 @@
     }
 
     // an absent or empty schema means any object
-    if (json_schema.is_object() && json_schema.empty()) {
+    //
+    // Not when the caller supplied a grammar: a schema beats a grammar
+    // downstream, so inventing one here would silently discard what they
+    // asked for. Left empty, the schema reads as "none" and the grammar wins.
+    if (grammar.empty() && json_schema.is_object() && json_schema.empty()) {
         json_schema["type"] = "object";
     }
 
